==Strategy==
Zeruel's stages are very tricky in nature. Once you build up your wallet and hit the base, lure Super Metal Hippoe, then kill it using Waitress Cat. Make sure when you do this that the Sniper the Cat powerup is not turned on to prevent anything bad happening. From then on, your main goal is to chip down Zeruel's massive HP while quickly killing the Metal Doges. Zeruel's Omni-Strike is extremely large, so make sure it doesn't gain any ground after it completes its attack. Because of Zeruel's ridiculously high health pool, this means that a clear of WARNING 14 will usually take around '''30''' minutes because your main sources of damage will most likely be Manic Lion, Bullet Train, and Awakened Bahamut once in a while.

If you have any EVA Angel Killer units, feel free to use them to make the process of chipping down each boss quicker.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]]: Riceball's fast attacks makes him the best meatshield to use here. Use Riceball at the start to allow Super Metal Hippoe and the Metal Doges to attack it while Waitress one-shots the Super Metal Hippoe. You won't need boosting nor Talents given Zeruel's ridiculously high damage.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut's high damage allows him to get extremely high damage against Zeruel if there aren't any Metal Doges in the way.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: Researcher's rapid attacks and speed allows him to work as a generalist Critter for the Metal Doges.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]: Cleanerbot is a strong staller here to keep Zeruel in place for a few seconds. Also helps for luring Super Metal Hippoe. Note that his True Form is not recommended because of its drastic Speed increase, making timing it to allow Waitress to one-shot Super Metal Hippoe a bit tougher. If you happen to have a free slot, a Speed Up Combo featuring Figure Skating Cats exists alongside Cleanerbot, which alongside its second form should make timing it very easy.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]]: Metal's...well, Metal attribute allows him to tank multiple Zeruel hits in a row. Try to protect him from Metal Doge's rapid attacks with Riceball or Manic Lion.
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]]: Manic Lion's rapid attacks and low cooldown allows him to work as a sufficient staller / chipper for Metal Doges.
*[[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] and [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]]: For players without Cat Researcher, the best way to kill the Metal Doges will be sending a bunch of Lions and hoping for the best. Because of this, it's not a terrible idea to add both normal Lion and Li'l Lion alongside Manic Lion for a triple lion death barrage against the Metal Doges. This does use up a lot of cash, so be careful when doing this.
*[[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]]: Instantly kills Super Metal Hippoe. You only need a level 30 Waitress to one-shot the Super Metal Hippoe.
*[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]]: A fast unit similar to Cat Researcher that kills the Metal Doges quickly.

