==Strategy==
What was once a genuinely hard stage now falls to the power of Bahamut's Talents. Simply lure the first Angelic Gory, beat it up with Bahamut, then spam low-range units like Slime, Manic Eraser, and Ramen. Because of The 9th Angel's blindspot, these units are free to wreck havoc without fear of retaliation. Any supporting peons that might've messed this up before die quickly to the outer parts of Bahamut's Explosion as well as Slime's Waves. If executed properly, it's possible to easily win without even using any EVA Angel Killer Ubers. Of course, bringing them is still recommended to speed up the fight while Bahamut keeps the peons occupied.

If you don't have Bahamut's Talents, this stage serves as a shining example of why Evangelion is classified as a psychological horror anime. With '''infinite''' 350% Angelic Gories and a high-range, high-health boss that tears apart anything that even dares to try entering its blindspot, you're going to need to pull out everything you've got for these last few stages. This is necessary because The 9th Angel has a whopping 9 million health and 270,000 damage that reaches all the way up to 750 range at the absolute most. Your main goal is to use Bahamut for the first Angelic Gory, then start chipping The 9th Angel down while you find more and more complex ways to kill each Angelic Gory.


==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Meatshields: Given the nature of these stages, you can't afford to use slower options like Eraser Cat. The best options here are [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]].
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: Supercar's low range means he can fit into The 9th Angel's blindspot comfortably, and his 81,000 damage racks up very quickly.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut's low range means he can fit into The 9th Angel's blindspot, and his Explosion, with a consistent spawn location, can deal extreme damage to both Angelic Gory and The 9th Angel. As mentioned before, Bahamut is critical to all non-Uber strategies with his raw damage keeping the peons in check while The 9th Angel remains helpless.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: Disposable nuke damage for dire situations.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]]: Your second Bahamut here, to be used if there's an Angelic Gory on screen and your Bahamut's still off cooldown.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: While Ramen won't do anything in the face of The 9th Angel nuke, he still works to stall Angelic Gory.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Slime is an extremely strong unit here, being able to abuse the peons to unleash high damage Wave attacks. Note that Slime's interaction with Gabriel is always a loss. If you have Slime's True Form, he becomes able to spread his Wave even further, as well as being able to connect onto Angelic Gory.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is a fast generalist attacker who can quickly deal with the Bloggers, Ginger Snaches, and Gabriels.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: A strong attacker who can deal very well against the Gabriels and Angelic Gories.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]]: Similar to Mushroom, but with higher stats and LD.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: A strong unit that can bait out The 9th Angel early on, and works to stall Angelic Gory later on.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: A strong unit for the supporting enemies here. Also can chip down Sachiel given proper timing.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Similar to Bullet Train Cat, being a faster attacker with good chip potential.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter Cat]]: Cutter has much lower damage than Bullet Train Cat, but has a Survive to allow him to get much higher damage in, especially against the Sir Seals or Ginger Snaches. Also has an Attack combo with Li'l Brave Cat.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Extremely useful unit to chip down The 9th Angel as well as the supporting peons. Can also abuse Trolly Blogger to get multiple rebounds.
*[[Rei Ayanami (Super Rare Cat)|Reunion Li'l Rei]]: Among the Super Rare EVA Angel Killers, Rei is designed to help beat these stages: Rei's stats are very high against Angels, with damage surpassing Mushroom's, and she can tank The 9th Angel.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Anti-Angel Ubers: Try to use options that are either disposable or fast. Examples include [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]], [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]] and [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]].
*Rushers: Examples include [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], [[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]] and [[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]].
